# Review package: batch 6, slice cert-delta

## ed08a4da Keep the link on http when the listener could not load its chain, and say why in the log

The fix round of batch 6's certificate slice. Each behaviour change starts from a test that failed for it.

mayRunHttps read only a chain's first block, while LinkListener.use loads the whole chain with createSecureContext. A
leaf with a broken or cut off second block gave https, and the link then stopped working in browsers. It now makes the
listener's own call as well, and keeps checkPrivateKey, because createSecureContext takes a key of another algorithm.

A date that cannot be read gave NaN, which passed the time check, so the check now asks for time left and NaN answers no.

linkMode swallowed every throw, so an operator whose link stayed on http had no trace of why. It now writes a warning
through loggable, which keeps no value an error was given. A test checks with booleans that no key reaches the line.

configFor took names every object inherits, such as toString, as a mode and wrote a proxy with no port. It now throws
unless the mode is the table's own name.

The fake relay kept a name's sync across its binding's delete, while the real relay drops sync with the binding
(BINDING_LIFETIME_TABLES). A name freed and bound again now starts with no sync record, in the fake as in the relay. Two
comments are corrected: the sync record's rule on the copy, and where the racing sign-in tries now run.

Ruling: linkMode takes an optional third argument log, writeTunnelSettings passes it on, PublicLinks.sync gives ctx.log, and the CLI and Task 8's status call give none - why: plan 1b's Interfaces and Task 8's manager call linkMode with two arguments, and a status read should not write a line per poll - cost if wrong: a broken row's reason reaches the log only from a sync, which runs at every lead start and link change
Ruling: the sync record's comment says a sync that is on names its copy and one that is off may name one or none - why: the brief's wording (a copy unless the state is off) does not match the refine, which lets a copy through in any state and agrees with relay.py's sync_copy - cost if wrong: a comment only

